 "transcript": {
  "answer": "Yes. Investors pay more than owner-occupiers on the standard variable rate, by about 0.58 percentage points.\n\nIn September 2026, the RBA's advertised indicator rates for banks were:\n- **Investor:** 9.35%\n- **Owner-occupier:** 8.77%\n\nThe gap was the same at the start of 2025, so it has been steady. In January 2025 the rates were 9.35% for investors and 8.77% for owner-occupiers. In August 2025 to January 2026 they were 8.60% and 8.02%. Both rates moved together through the cuts in 2025 and the rises in 2026.\n\nThese are advertised standard variable rates. Most borrowers pay less than that because of discounts, and the RBA's discounted-rate series would show the gap on those loans. Actual rates paid on new loans are in the RBA's F6 table, and I haven't pulled that here.",
